+          "category": "\ud83d\udc51 Pixaroma/\ud83c\udfb5 Audio",
+          "description": "For MiniMax H3 videos LONGER than about 15 seconds: 30 seconds, a minute or more, made in one run with no joins. For 15 seconds or less you do not need it (with it, nothing changes). Put it on the model wire before H3 Audio Sync and the sampler, and set the video length you need, up to about 149 seconds (ComfyUI's own MiniMax H3 nodes stop at 3600 frames).\n\nH3 was trained on clips of up to about 15 seconds. This node still makes the whole video as one piece, but on every step the model looks at it in overlapping windows of about 10 seconds, each with its own part of your song, and the windows are blended where they overlap. Because every window is worked on at every step, they agree with each other and there is no seam, flash or quality drop anywhere.\n\nIt also needs far less graphics memory than one long run and is faster: a minute at 864 took 4.5 minutes instead of 9.4 on a 4090, and with only 12 GB of graphics memory free it ran at the same speed (a minute at 864, and 30 seconds at 1024), where one long run could not finish a step.\n\nThis node only works with MiniMax H3. Find it by searching for h3, minimax, long video, windows.",
